\subsection{Industrial oven}
Minute-to-minute moves are almost uncorrelated, including inside one chamber, and about 82\% of minutes do not change by a whole degree. There is little cross-sensor agreement for removal to use. Persistence is strong, so the three-tap trend residual removes about 40\% of the ordinary step. The earliest 70\% holds 1{,}444{,}885 one-minute windows. The fit keeps 40{,}000 of them, spaced across that period. The later pool holds 619{,}295 windows. Each seed keeps 4{,}000 for the thresholds and the cutoff, and 4{,}000 for the rates in Table~\ref{tab:oven}. The ten-minute window is capped the same way.

